# File structure

## Components — folder + index.tsx only

- Each component lives in its own PascalCase folder; implementation is `index.tsx`.
- Next to it when needed: `types.ts`, `styles.module.css`, `hooks/`, `components/` (nested).
- Never create a component as a lone `.ts` / `.tsx` file in the parent folder.

```
src/components/CroppedText/
  index.tsx
  types.ts
  styles.module.css
```

## Split by content type

- Constants → `consts/` (or `consts.ts` / `consts/index.ts` inside a feature).
- Types → `types/` (or local `types.ts` if used only by that component).
- Utilities → `utils/`.
- Hooks → `hooks/`.
- Do not mix: no constants in component files, no types inside utils, etc.

## Component props — OwnProps → Props

- Define local `OwnProps` in `types.ts`; export `Props = FC<OwnProps>`.
- Component: `const Foo: Props = (...) => { ... }`.
- Do not export `OwnProps`. Reuse via `ComponentProps<typeof Foo>`, `Parameters<Props>[0]`, or a shared type in `types/`.
- Do not type as `React.FC<...>` inline in `index.tsx` or `function Foo(props: SomeProps)`.

```ts
import type { FC } from 'react';

type OwnProps = {
  text: string | undefined;
  length?: number;
};

export type Props = FC<OwnProps>;
```

## Extensions

- React components — always `.tsx`.
- Pure TS (no JSX) — `.ts`.
- Styles — `.module.css` (CSS modules).

## No barrel re-exports

- Do not add `index.ts` whose only job is re-exporting siblings.
- Import the concrete `index.tsx` / `utils.ts` / `consts.ts` directly.
